('127.101.d.11.A',3,'Base cabinets are usually about how deep?','["48 inches", "24 inches", "12 inches", "6 inches"]'::jsonb,1,'Standard base depth is 24 inches.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.A',4,'Wall cabinets are commonly:','["48 inches deep", "24 inches deep", "12 inches deep", "36 inches deep"]'::jsonb,2,'Wall cabinets are shallower.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.B',3,'The part of a cabinet that holds the doors is the:','["Toe kick", "Counter", "Backsplash", "Face frame"]'::jsonb,3,'Face frames hold doors.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.B',4,'Concealed hinges are chosen for cabinets for their:','["Adjustability and clean look", "Noise", "Squeaks", "Rust"]'::jsonb,0,'Euro hinges adjust.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.C',3,'Before installing countertops, base cabinets must be:','["Loose", "Level and fastened together", "Painted", "Empty of screws"]'::jsonb,1,'Level cabinets support tops.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.C',4,'Backsplashes are installed to protect the wall from:','["Sound", "Light", "Water and splashes", "Heat only"]'::jsonb,2,'Backsplashes protect walls.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.D',3,'An island base cabinet is secured to the floor with:','["Glue only", "Tape", "Rope", "Cleats or screws"]'::jsonb,3,'Islands are anchored to prevent tipping.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.D',4,'An island should allow clearances of about:','["36 to 42 inches around it", "6 inches", "12 inches", "100 inches"]'::jsonb,0,'Clearance allows movement.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.E',3,'Cabinets are commonly made from hardwoods such as:','["Pine only", "Oak and maple", "Balsa", "Cardboard"]'::jsonb,1,'Oak and maple are durable.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.E',4,'Plywood is used for cabinet boxes because it is:','["Weak", "Heavy", "Stable and strong", "Flammable"]'::jsonb,2,'Plywood resists warping.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.F',3,'A strong cabinetmaking joint is the:','["Staple joint", "Butt joint with no glue", "Tape joint", "Dovetail"]'::jsonb,3,'Dovetails interlock.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.F',4,'A dado joint is a:','["Groove cut across the grain to receive a board", "Mitered corner", "Glued edge", "Pin"]'::jsonb,0,'Dadoes hold shelves.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.G',3,'Before building a cabinet from drawings, the builder should make a:','["Joke list", "Cut list", "Nap list", "Wish list"]'::jsonb,1,'Cut lists organize parts.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.G',4,'When assembling a cabinet box, clamps are used to:','["Add weight", "Decorate", "Hold parts square while glue dries", "Stain wood"]'::jsonb,2,'Clamps keep pressure.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.H',4,'After applying laminate, the edges are trimmed flush with a:','["Plane", "Hammer", "Saw", "Router"]'::jsonb,3,'Routers trim edges.','original'),
('127.101.d.7.C',3,'Which finishing tool applies joint compound with a rolling, pressurized head instead of a hand knife?','["Automatic taper or compound tube", "Utility blade", "Hawk and trowel", "Putty knife"]'::jsonb,0,'Power taping tools apply mud quickly.','original'),
('127.101.d.7.C',4,'A corner finisher is an automatic tool designed to:','["Set tile", "Apply and smooth compound in inside corners", "Cut studs", "Hang boards"]'::jsonb,1,'Corner tools finish inside angles.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.H',3,'When laminating a countertop, the contact cement is applied to:','["Neither surface", "Only the floor", "Both the laminate and the substrate", "Only the laminate edge"]'::jsonb,2,'Both surfaces need cement.','original'),
('127.101.d.11.H',4,'After the contact cement becomes tacky and the laminate is positioned, the installer presses it with a:','["Chisel", "Trowel", "Paintbrush", "J-roller"]'::jsonb,3,'Rolling ensures complete bond.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
